================================================================================

    n = band index.
  Emf = "inner" mean-field energy eigenvalue used to construct Sigma(E),
        read from WFN_inner.
   Eo = "outer" mean-field energy eigenvalue where we center the evaluation
        frequency grid {E} of Sigma(E). Defaults to Emf, unless
        you use WFN_outer and eqp_outer.dat / scissors_outer.
  Vxc = exchange-correlation pot., calculated from VXC or read from vxc.dat.
  KIH = Kinetic energy + Ionic potential + Hartree, read from kih.dat.
    X = bare exchange.
  Res = residue contrib. to Sigma(E) at energy E=Eo.
  Int = contrib. to Sigma(E) at energy E=Eo due to integral over imag. freqs.
  Cor = Res + Int = correlation portion of Sigma(E) at energy E=Eo.
  Sig = X + Cor = self energy Sigma(E) at energy E=Eo.
 Eqp0 = on-shell QP energy = Emf - Vxc + Sig(Eo)
        Eqp0 is *not* the recommended quantity to use for QP properties.
 Eqp1 = off-shell solution to the linearized  Dyson`s equation
      = Eqp0 + (dSig/dE) / (1 - dSig/dE) * (Eqp0 - Eo),
        or a full linear interpolation if more freq. points where computed.
        Eqp1 is the recommended quantity to use for QP properties.
 Soln = Whether we found a solution to Dyson`s equation for Eqp1 (see notes).
  Znk = quasiparticle renormalization factor

 Notes on the solutions to Dyson`s equation (Soln):
 - When we solve Dyson`s eqn. for Eqp1, we might find several or no roots.
 - If Soln=unique, there is only one solution and the answer is unambiguous
 - If Soln=extrap{-/+}, we found a solution by extrapolating Sigma(E) to values of
   E smaller/greater than our frequency grid. PROCEED WITH CAUTION
 - If Soln=MULT:, there are multiple solutions to Dyson`s equation. We
   report the solution closer to Eqp0. PROCEED WITH CAUTION
 - If Soln=NO_SOLN!, there is no solution and extrap. is not possible. This
   can happen if your frequency grid for Sigma is too small, and Sigma(E) is
   ill-behaved. We simply copy Eqp0 to Eqp1, so DON`T TRUST THE ANSWER.
 - The number of sols. in full-freq. calcs. is affected by self-consistently
   updating the eigenvalues in WFN_inner. Consider reruning your calculation
   with eqp or scissors corrections if you have many unstable solutions.

 General notes:
 - All energies are reported here in eV.
 - Both Emf and Vxc contain the average pot. Vxc0, so Vxc0 doesn`t affect Sigma.
 - Eqp1 and Eqp0 are Eqs. (36-37) from Hybertsen & Louie PRB 34 5390.
 - We recommend you use Eqp1 for QP properties of materials.

